  "id": "functional-asymmetry",
  "term": "functional asymmetry",
  "definition": "Functional asymmetry is the unequal activation or specialization of the brain’s two hemispheres during a mental function. In this account, stronger activity in one hemisphere can inhibit the matching area on the other side through the corpus callosum, producing a left- or right-sided pattern of processing.",
